    "metadata": {
     "title": "Upper Bound and Dynamic Evolution Mechanism of Gold Reserve Ratios under a Credit Money System | 信用货币体系下黄金占总官方储备资产比例的理论上限",
     "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22135513",
     "publication_date": "2026-08-28",
     "description": "<p>本文建立了一个基于全球合并央行资产负债表的宏观动态模型,严密推导了信用货币体系下黄金占官方总储备资产比例的理论上限及其长期演化规律。研究表明,由于全球名义经济与主权债务规模呈指数复利增长,其增速远超物理黄金的开采极限,若要维持黄金在总资产中的固定比例,金价年化涨幅必须强制高于主权债务名义利率。这将破坏金融市场的跨期无套利条件,引发全网对主权信用债务的抛售与对黄金的挤兑,直接导致信用体系崩塌。因此,信用货币体系的生存前提是黄金占官方总储备比例在长期呈现单调递减趋势。</p>\n<p>This paper establishes a macroeconomic dynamic model based on the global consolidated central bank balance sheet to rigorously derive the theoretical upper bound and long-term evolutionary path of the proportion of gold in official total reserve assets under a credit money system. The research demonstrates that because nominal global economic output and sovereign debt expand at an exponential compound rate far exceeding the physical extraction limits of gold, maintaining a fixed proportion of gold in total assets requires the annual nominal appreciation rate of gold to strictly exceed the nominal interest rate on sovereign debt. This condition breaks the intertemporal no-arbitrage condition in financial markets, inducing a systemic sell-off of sovereign credit debt and a run on physical gold, ultimately triggering a collapse of the credit system. Consequently, the survival of a credit money system necessitates that the proportion of gold in official reserves monotonically approaches zero over time.&nbsp;</p>",
